---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { SettingsListPlayground, SettingsListRows } from '../../components/SettingsListDemo';
---

<Docs title="Settings List">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Settings List</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Titled groups of settings. Each row names a setting, explains it, and puts its value or control beside it.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <SettingsListPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Settings list usage"
      code={`import { SettingsGroup, SettingsRow } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/settings-list";

<SettingsGroup title="Profile" titleId="profile-heading">
  <SettingsRow label="Email" description="Used to sign in.">
    <span className="break-all">{user.email}</span>
  </SettingsRow>
  <SettingsRow
    label="Name"
    htmlFor="account-name"
    description={<span id="account-name-help">Up to 80 characters.</span>}
  >
    <Input id="account-name" aria-describedby="account-name-help" />
  </SettingsRow>
</SettingsGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>SettingsGroup</code> renders a <code>section</code> with a title and a bordered panel. Pass{' '}
      <code>titleId</code> to name the section by its title; leave it out for lists that repeat, like one group per
      table. The title is an
      <code>h2</code>; set <code>heading</code> to <code>"h3"</code> or <code>"h4"</code> when the group sits under
      another heading.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SettingsRow</code> takes a <code>label</code>, an optional
      <code>description</code>, and children for the value or control. With
      <code>htmlFor</code>, the label is a real <code>label</code>, so clicking it focuses the control. A row without
      children has no control area, which suits read-only facts like a role or a directory entry.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Rows</h2>
    <p>
      Rows stack text over the control in narrow groups. From 36rem of group width, the control moves to the right and
      takes at most 60% of the row. Controls wrap; long text and codes break instead of overflowing.
    </p>
    <SettingsListRows client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Notes, forms, and alerts</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Other children in a group"
      code={`<SettingsGroup title="Workspace identity" titleId="identity-heading">
  {!admin && <p className="px-[var(--sprout-settings-row-inline)] py-[var(--sprout-settings-row-block)]">
    Only workspace admins can rename or close this workspace.
  </p>}
  <form onSubmit={save}>
    <SettingsRow label="Workspace name" htmlFor="workspace-name">…</SettingsRow>
    {dirty && <div className="flex justify-end gap-2 px-4 pb-3">…</div>}
  </form>
  {saved && <p role="status">Workspace name saved.</p>}
</SettingsGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      Any child can sit in a group, and every child gets a divider above it. Children that render nothing add no
      divider. Notes and blocks can match row padding with <code>--sprout-settings-row-inline</code> and
      <code>--sprout-settings-row-block</code>. Pick the Workspace and Account pages in the playground to see forms,
      save messages, a conflict alert, and loading or error states inside rows.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Name controls with <code>htmlFor</code>, or pass your own
      <code>label</code> element as the label. Link help text with
      <code>aria-describedby</code> by giving the description an id. The list has no motion of its own. Switches,
      checkboxes, the text field, and the theme toggle in these examples are docs-only stand-ins; data and saving are
      sample code.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
